[[2047,15,65536,"<h3>Functional description</h3><p>The radio \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is supplied directly\n(pins 4 and 7 of connector A) by the battery via the line for fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F10</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of\nthe junction unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               and maxifuse J/B1 of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B99</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>It receives a supply when the ignition is\nswitched on (INT) (pin 3 of connector A) via the line for fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of\nthe junction unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>With the side lights switched on, the supply\nreaches pin 6 of connector A by means of the line coming from the\nswitch for the steering column switch unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>H5</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , protected\nby fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F4</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of the additional fuse box \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B98B</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ; the radio\ncontrols are therefore lit up when the side lights are switched\non.</p><p>Pin 8 of connector A, on the other hand,\nis earthed (\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>C20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              ).</p><p>Pin 5 of connector A is connected to the\ncontrol unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P22</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               which controls the aerial built into the\nspoiler. The control unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P22</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               is then connected to the radio by\nmeans of the specific aerial lead.</p><p>Connector B sends out cables carrying signals to the speakers:</p><ul><li>pins 5 and 6 to the left front speakers <strong>P35</strong> and <strong>P45</strong> ;</li><li>pins 3 and 4 to the right front loudspeakers <strong>P36</strong> and <strong>P46</strong> ;</li><li>pins 7 and 8 to the left rear speakers <strong>P30</strong> and <strong>P40</strong> ,\nand to the subwoofer <strong>P92</strong> ;</li><li>pins 1 and 2 to the right rear speakers <strong>P31</strong> and <strong>P41</strong> ,\nand to the subwoofer <strong>P92</strong> ;</li></ul><p>The subwoofer \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P92</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               has its own supply\nwhich arrives directly from the line protected by fuse \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>F8</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               of\nthe junction unit \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>B1</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              , and is connected to pin 5 of connector\nA of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p><p>The connecting cable to the CD player \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P75</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                               comes\nout of connector C of \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              <strong>P20</strong>\n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              \n                              .</p>"]]